IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa8-helpers`

-- coa8-part14-meanings.l4: Companies Act 2006, Part 14 (control of political donations and expenditure),
-- ss 362 to 365: what the Part is about and the meanings it gives (lines 4656-4692 of ukpga-2006-46.txt).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. The seat layer is coa8-seat.l4.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer; see NOTES.md, "Reading a result").
--   JUST TRUE   the text says the case is within the term.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words (a "means" definition, an "if" or "only if", a flat negative).
--               Each such branch carries  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<the quoted words>"
--   NOTHING     the text does not decide it (silent, list not closed, includes, undefined term, points outside the
--               text, limited by its own wording). Each such branch carries  -- NOTHING-kind (<why>)
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
--
-- s 362 (Introductory) is inert: reason 1 (a purpose clause that creates no rule); see NOTES.md.

§ `Part 14: Control of political donations and expenditure`

§§ `Donations and expenditure to which this Part applies`

-- ---- s 363: political parties, organisations etc to which this Part applies ---------------------------------

-- src:4664 | (1) This Part applies to a political party if it is registered under Part 2 of the Political Parties, Elections and Referendums Act 2000 (c. 41).
@ref s 363(1) Political parties, organisations etc to which this Part applies (src:4664)
GIVEN `registered under Part 2 of the Political Parties, Elections and Referendums Act 2000` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 363(1) this Part applies to the political party` MEANS
    IF `registered under Part 2 of the Political Parties, Elections and Referendums Act 2000`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Part applies to a political party if it is registered"

-- src:4668 | (3) This Part applies to an independent election candidate at any election to public office held in the United Kingdom ....
@ref s 363(3) Independent election candidates (src:4668)
GIVEN `standing at an election to public office held in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 363(3) this Part applies to the independent election candidate` MEANS
    IF `standing at an election to public office held in the United Kingdom`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "at any election to public office held in the United Kingdom"

-- (2)(a): the activities are capable of being reasonably regarded as intended to affect public support for a party or
-- candidate to which this Part applies. "Capable of being reasonably regarded" is an open-textured judgment: a plain input.
-- src:4665 | (2) This Part applies to an organisation (a “political organisation”) if it carries on, or proposes to carry on, activities that are capable of being reasonably regarded as intended—
-- src:4666 | (a) to affect public support for a political party to which, or an independent election candidate to whom, this Part applies, or
@ref s 363(2)(a) Activities intended to affect public support (src:4665-4666)
GIVEN `capable of being reasonably regarded as intended to affect public support for the party or candidate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this Part applies to that party or candidate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 363(2)(a) the activities are intended to affect public support for a party or candidate to which this Part applies` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it carries on, or proposes to carry on, activities that are capable of being reasonably regarded as intended"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where `this Part applies to that party or candidate` is NOTHING
    `s 362 helper both answers` (JUST `capable of being reasonably regarded as intended to affect public support for the party or candidate`) `this Part applies to that party or candidate`

-- src:4667 | (b) to influence voters in relation to any national or regional referendum held under the law of the United Kingdom ....
@ref s 363(2)(b) Activities intended to influence referendum voters (src:4667)
GIVEN `capable of being reasonably regarded as intended to influence voters in relation to a national or regional referendum held under the law of the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 363(2)(b) the activities are intended to influence voters in a referendum` MEANS
    IF `capable of being reasonably regarded as intended to influence voters in relation to a national or regional referendum held under the law of the United Kingdom`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it carries on, or proposes to carry on, activities that are capable of being reasonably regarded as intended"

-- src:4665 | (2) This Part applies to an organisation (a “political organisation”) if it carries on, or proposes to carry on, activities that are capable of being reasonably regarded as intended—
-- src:4666 | (a) to affect public support for a political party to which, or an independent election candidate to whom, this Part applies, or
-- src:4667 | (b) to influence voters in relation to any national or regional referendum held under the law of the United Kingdom ....
@ref s 363(2) Political organisation (src:4665-4667)
GIVEN `carries on, or proposes to carry on, activities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `limb (a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `limb (b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 363(2) the organisation is a political organisation` MEANS
    IF `carries on, or proposes to carry on, activities`
    THEN `s 362 helper either answer` `limb (a)` `limb (b)`
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it carries on, or proposes to carry on, activities that are capable of being reasonably regarded as intended"

-- (4): a rule of reading, over a small typed representation of what a later reference is to.
-- Each kind of thing is judged by the rule that says when this Part applies to it.
-- src:4669 | (4) Any reference in the following provisions of this Part to a political party, political organisation or independent election candidate, or to political expenditure, is to a party, organisation, independent candidate or expenditure to which this Part applies.
@ref s 363(4) References in the later provisions of this Part (the things referred to) (src:4669)
DECLARE `s 363(4) thing referred to` IS ONE OF
    `s 363(4) a political party`
        HAS `s 363(4) the party is registered under Part 2 of the Political Parties, Elections and Referendums Act 2000` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 363(4) a political organisation`
        HAS `s 363(4) the organisation carries on, or proposes to carry on, activities` IS A BOOLEAN
            `s 363(4) its activities are capable of being reasonably regarded as intended to affect public support` IS A BOOLEAN
            `s 363(4) the party or candidate whose support is affected is one to which this Part applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
            `s 363(4) its activities are capable of being reasonably regarded as intended to influence voters in a referendum` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 363(4) an independent election candidate`
        HAS `s 363(4) the candidate is standing at an election to public office held in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 363(4) political expenditure`
        HAS `s 363(4) the expenditure is political expenditure within section 365(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN

@ref s 363(4) References in the later provisions of this Part (src:4669)
GIVEN thing IS A `s 363(4) thing referred to`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 363(4) the reference is to a party, organisation, candidate or expenditure to which this Part applies` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `s 363(4) a political party` registered THEN `s 363(1) this Part applies to the political party` registered
    WHEN `s 363(4) a political organisation` carries capable applies referendum THEN
        `s 363(2) the organisation is a political organisation` carries
            (`s 363(2)(a) the activities are intended to affect public support for a party or candidate to which this Part applies` capable applies)
            (`s 363(2)(b) the activities are intended to influence voters in a referendum` referendum)
    WHEN `s 363(4) an independent election candidate` standing THEN `s 363(3) this Part applies to the independent election candidate` standing
    WHEN `s 363(4) political expenditure` within THEN within -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where section 365(1) answers NOTHING

-- ---- s 364: meaning of "political donation" ------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 364(1) is a lead-in ("The following provisions have effect ... as regards the meaning"): inert, reason 1 (fork F1).
-- The text hands the meaning to sections 50 to 53 of the Political Parties, Elections and Referendums Act 2000, which are not
-- among the sources: each borrowed answer is an input, MAYBE BOOLEAN (NOTHING where it is not known).

-- src:4682 | (4) For the purposes of this section, sections 50 and 53 of the Political Parties, Elections and Referendums Act 2000 (c. 41) (definition of “donation” and value of donations) shall be treated as if the amendments to those sections made by the Electoral Administration Act 2006 (which remove from the definition of “donation” loans made otherwise than on commercial terms) had not been made.
@ref s 364(4) Sections 50 and 53 treated as if the Electoral Administration Act 2006 amendments had not been made (src:4682)
GIVEN `as sections 50 and 53 now stand` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `as sections 50 and 53 would stand if the amendments made by the Electoral Administration Act 2006 had not been made` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 364(4) the answer under sections 50 and 53 to use for this section` MEANS
    `as sections 50 and 53 would stand if the amendments made by the Electoral Administration Act 2006 had not been made`

-- src:4672 | (2) In relation to a political party or other political organisation—
-- src:4673 | (a) “political donation” means anything that in accordance with sections 50 to 52 of the Political Parties, Elections and Referendums Act 2000—
-- src:4674 | (i) constitutes a donation for the purposes of Chapter 1 of Part 4 of that Act (control of donations to registered parties), or
-- src:4675 | (ii) would constitute such a donation reading references in those sections to a registered party as references to any political party or other political organisation,
-- src:4676 | and
-- src:4677 | (b) section 53 of that Act applies, in the same way, for the purpose of determining the value of a donation.
@ref s 364(2)(a) Political donation: political party or other political organisation (src:4672-4677)
GIVEN `constitutes a donation for the purposes of Chapter 1 of Part 4 of that Act` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `would constitute such a donation reading references to a registered party as references to any political party or other political organisation` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 364(2)(a) the thing is a political donation to the political party or other political organisation` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“political donation” means anything that in accordance with sections 50 to 52"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where a borrowed answer is not known
    `s 362 helper either answer`
        `constitutes a donation for the purposes of Chapter 1 of Part 4 of that Act`
        `would constitute such a donation reading references to a registered party as references to any political party or other political organisation`

-- src:4672 | (2) In relation to a political party or other political organisation—
-- src:4673 | (a) “political donation” means anything that in accordance with sections 50 to 52 of the Political Parties, Elections and Referendums Act 2000—
-- src:4674 | (i) constitutes a donation for the purposes of Chapter 1 of Part 4 of that Act (control of donations to registered parties), or
-- src:4675 | (ii) would constitute such a donation reading references in those sections to a registered party as references to any political party or other political organisation,
-- src:4676 | and
-- src:4677 | (b) section 53 of that Act applies, in the same way, for the purpose of determining the value of a donation.
@ref s 364(2)(b) Value of the donation: section 53 (src:4672-4677)
GIVEN `the value of the donation as section 53 of the Political Parties, Elections and Referendums Act 2000 determines it, in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 364(2)(b) the value of the donation for this Part` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the value of the donation as section 53 of the Political Parties, Elections and Referendums Act 2000 determines it, in pounds`
    WHEN JUST v THEN JUST v
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "section 53 of that Act applies, in the same way, for the purpose of determining the value of a donation"

-- src:4678 | (3) In relation to an independent election candidate—
-- src:4679 | (a) “political donation” means anything that, in accordance with sections 50 to 52 of that Act, would constitute a donation for the purposes of Chapter 1 of Part 4 of that Act (control of donations to registered parties) reading references in those sections to a registered party as references to the independent election candidate,
-- src:4680 | and
-- src:4681 | (b) section 53 of that Act applies, in the same way, for the purpose of determining the value of a donation.
@ref s 364(3)(a) Political donation: independent election candidate (src:4678-4681)
GIVEN `would constitute a donation for the purposes of Chapter 1 of Part 4 reading references to a registered party as references to the independent election candidate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 364(3)(a) the thing is a political donation to the independent election candidate` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“political donation” means anything that, in accordance with sections 50 to 52 of that Act, would constitute a donation"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where the borrowed answer is not known
    `would constitute a donation for the purposes of Chapter 1 of Part 4 reading references to a registered party as references to the independent election candidate`

-- src:4678 | (3) In relation to an independent election candidate—
-- src:4679 | (a) “political donation” means anything that, in accordance with sections 50 to 52 of that Act, would constitute a donation for the purposes of Chapter 1 of Part 4 of that Act (control of donations to registered parties) reading references in those sections to a registered party as references to the independent election candidate,
-- src:4680 | and
-- src:4681 | (b) section 53 of that Act applies, in the same way, for the purpose of determining the value of a donation.
@ref s 364(3)(b) Value of the donation to an independent election candidate (src:4678-4681)
GIVEN `the value of the donation as section 53 determines it, in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 364(3)(b) the value of the donation to the independent election candidate for this Part` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the value of the donation as section 53 determines it, in pounds`
    WHEN JUST v THEN JUST v
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "section 53 of that Act applies, in the same way, for the purpose of determining the value of a donation"

-- ---- s 365: meaning of "political expenditure" ---------------------------------------------------------------
-- (1)(a)(i) "of whatever nature" and (1)(a)(ii) "however published or otherwise disseminated" add no condition: no input.

-- src:4684 | (1) In this Part “political expenditure”, in relation to a company, means expenditure incurred by the company on—
-- src:4685 | (a) the preparation, publication or dissemination of advertising or other promotional or publicity material—
-- src:4686 | (i) of whatever nature, and
-- src:4687 | (ii) however published or otherwise disseminated,
-- src:4688 | that, at the time of publication or dissemination, is capable of being reasonably regarded as intended to affect public support for a political party or other political organisation, or an independent election candidate, or
@ref s 365(1)(a) Political expenditure: advertising and publicity material (src:4684-4688)
GIVEN `incurred by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on the preparation, publication or dissemination of advertising or other promotional or publicity material` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the time of publication or dissemination the material is capable of being reasonably regarded as intended to affect public support for a political party or other political organisation, or an independent election candidate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this Part applies to that party, organisation or candidate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 365(1)(a) the expenditure is on advertising or publicity material intended to affect public support` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“political expenditure”, in relation to a company, means expenditure incurred by the company on"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where section 363(4) answers NOTHING for the party, organisation or candidate
    `s 362 helper both answers` (JUST `incurred by the company`)
        (`s 362 helper both answers` (JUST `on the preparation, publication or dissemination of advertising or other promotional or publicity material`)
            (`s 362 helper both answers` (JUST `at the time of publication or dissemination the material is capable of being reasonably regarded as intended to affect public support for a political party or other political organisation, or an independent election candidate`)
                `this Part applies to that party, organisation or candidate`))

-- src:4689 | (b) activities on the part of the company that are capable of being reasonably regarded as intended—
-- src:4690 | (i) to affect public support for a political party or other political organisation, or an independent election candidate, or
-- src:4691 | (ii) to influence voters in relation to any national or regional referendum held under the law of the United Kingdom.
@ref s 365(1)(b) Political expenditure: activities (src:4689-4691)
GIVEN `incurred by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on activities on the part of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the activities are capable of being reasonably regarded as intended to affect public support for a political party or other political organisation, or an independent election candidate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this Part applies to that party, organisation or candidate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the activities are capable of being reasonably regarded as intended to influence voters in a national or regional referendum held under the law of the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 365(1)(b) the expenditure is on activities intended to affect public support or to influence referendum voters` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means expenditure incurred by the company on"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where section 363(4) answers NOTHING for the party, organisation or candidate
    `s 362 helper both answers` (JUST `incurred by the company`)
        (`s 362 helper both answers` (JUST `on activities on the part of the company`)
            (`s 362 helper either answer`
                (`s 362 helper both answers` (JUST `the activities are capable of being reasonably regarded as intended to affect public support for a political party or other political organisation, or an independent election candidate`) `this Part applies to that party, organisation or candidate`)
                (JUST `the activities are capable of being reasonably regarded as intended to influence voters in a national or regional referendum held under the law of the United Kingdom`)))

-- src:4684 | (1) In this Part “political expenditure”, in relation to a company, means expenditure incurred by the company on—
-- src:4685 | (a) the preparation, publication or dissemination of advertising or other promotional or publicity material—
-- src:4686 | (i) of whatever nature, and
-- src:4687 | (ii) however published or otherwise disseminated,
-- src:4688 | that, at the time of publication or dissemination, is capable of being reasonably regarded as intended to affect public support for a political party or other political organisation, or an independent election candidate, or
-- src:4689 | (b) activities on the part of the company that are capable of being reasonably regarded as intended—
-- src:4690 | (i) to affect public support for a political party or other political organisation, or an independent election candidate, or
-- src:4691 | (ii) to influence voters in relation to any national or regional referendum held under the law of the United Kingdom.
@ref s 365(1) Meaning of "political expenditure" (src:4684-4691)
GIVEN `limb (a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `limb (b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 365(1) the expenditure is political expenditure` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this Part “political expenditure”, in relation to a company, means expenditure incurred by the company on"
    `s 362 helper either answer` `limb (a)` `limb (b)`

-- src:4692 | (2) For the purposes of this Part a political donation does not count as political expenditure.
@ref s 365(2) A political donation does not count as political expenditure (src:4692)
GIVEN `the spending is a political donation` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the spending is political expenditure within section 365(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 365(2) the spending counts as political expenditure` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the spending is a political donation`
    WHEN JUST x THEN
        IF x
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a political donation does not count as political expenditure"
        ELSE `the spending is political expenditure within section 365(1)`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER `the spending is political expenditure within section 365(1)`
        WHEN JUST y THEN
            IF y
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the spending is a political donation is not known
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means expenditure incurred by the company on"
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text)
